{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.e991458c263a94343322e33e.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"This proposal answers only whether either classification route stated in the retained circular is satisfied for a fund within its defined scope.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e991458c263a94343322e33e.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"All facts refer to the same assessment occasion. The packet does not supply the governing assessment date or measurement protocol.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e991458c263a94343322e33e.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The threshold fact is supplied only after the applicable exposure basis has been established; it is not inferred from the existence of private-market exposure or from disclosure examples.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e991458c263a94343322e33e.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"An operative SFC designation requires evidence of the SFC's decision. Risk factors, consultation, closer scrutiny and missing records do not establish or negate that decision.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e991458c263a94343322e33e.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"A false scope excludes the fund from this selected control; it does not classify the fund as non-complex under another regime.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":"58c57271fe995cd31b8d3fa7d190721a5c50503976bfb492a113dd370d0af7fa","candidate_id":"candidate.39dbe0b454f940f49ef275a2410e6bbd","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For an in-scope Fund, true means the retained circular's selected complex-product classification condition is satisfied: aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure is at least 50% of NAV, or an operative SFC case-specific designation applies. The Fund must then be treated as complex for distribution under this control. False means both routes are established to be absent at the assessment occasion; it does not establish non-complex status under all other rules. Missing exposure or designation evidence remains unknown unless a known satisfied route already determines the result. This predicate does not assess compliance with the resulting sale requirements.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["modality"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":["issue.7c30bbe0d2e741f78d8d2fcd93d70ee1","issue.e197e21ee37840898ad93034e4db728e","issue.0cf0ec04c68541a681dd691399c7de07","issue.0b652f68df184a2f97a6807fa8411eaf","issue.a8590855b032408b8546856f11c682d1"],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The source supports two distinct routes, rather than two rival interpretations of the 50% rule: automatic classification at or above 50%, and discretionary SFC designation below it. Below-threshold exposure alone does not establish non-complex status. The strongest unresolved interpretive issue is the exposure measurement basis: current exposure and permitted exposure can yield different threshold outcomes, but the packet does not adequately specify a competing executable measurement rule.","run_id":"run.2c02377eac73403ab71357020a633439","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"be86c12a28ac1c552b9cc386dfa44174629a63a786068d9bf5d8cdb44cbfa056","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u1.5","d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Selected control: complex-product classification for distribution under the retained circular"}